
* ip = (inv(T))'*im
* vp = T*vm
* im = T'*ip
* vm = inv(T)*vp
* Lm = inv(T)*L*inv(T');
* Cm = T'*C*T;
* Rm = inv(T)*R*inv(T');


* P = vp'*ip = vm'*im (power invariance)
* vp=T*vm
* annahme ip=S*im
* p=vp'*ip
* p=(T*vm)'(S*im)
* p=vm'*T'*S*im=vm'*Im
* T'*S have to be the eye-matrix I to let left and right side be the same
* T'*S=I -> S=inv(T')=(inv(T))'
* Probe:
* P=vp'*ip=(Tvm)'*(inv(T))'*im = vm'*T'*inv(T)'*im = vm'*im (OK!) (T'*inv(T)'=1)
*
* dVp/dx = -R*Ip -L*d(Ip/dt)
* und dIp/dx = -C*d(Vp/dt)
* mit Vp = T*Vm und Ip = inv(T)'*Im
* d(Vm/dx) = -inv(T)*R*inv(T)'*Im - inv(T)*L*inv(T)'*d(Im/dt) (inv(T)*R*inv(T)'=Rm , inv(T)*L*inv(T)'=Lm) UND
* und d(Im/dx) = -T'*C*T*d(Vm/dt) (T'*C*T=Cm)



* see also stalu_u110_o185mm2 matlab file for the DATA 
